  "id": "coldshoulder",
  "neon": "#8fe3ff",
  "note": "An ice house with no shopfront in it. The walls are the building: brick, then cork, then boards, so the door sits at the back of a reveal deep enough to stand in and the only openings above it are the louvre bank the store breathes through. The back half stands out over the Basin on a timber loading stage, which is where the ice leaves and the only part of the plot that is not masonry.",
